        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "28f80551-8cfa-577c-ae83-e0c5fe73184b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosemary Willis, John F. Kennedy\n- Places: Dealey Plaza, downtown Dallas, Texas, West End district\n- Events: Assassination of John F. Kennedy, Zapruder film\n\nFacts:\n- On November 22, 1963, Dealey Plaza in the historic West End district of downtown Dallas, Texas, was the location of the assassination of John F. Kennedy.\n- At the start of the assassination, Rosemary Willis was clearly visible in the Zapruder film wearing a white hooded coat and a red skirt.\n- During the assassination, Rosemary Willis trotted on the grass in Dealey Plaza to the left of the presidential limousine.\n- During the assassination, Rosemary Willis ran southwestward parallel with the presidential limousine and briefly faced it when the limousine was directly to her right.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b665d9ed-58df-5028-a018-9ed96bb6aa8f",
        "text": "Page: Rosemary Willis. Sentence: Clearly seen in the Zapruder film at the start of the assassination wearing a white, hooded coat and a red skirt, while she trotted in the Dealey Plaza grass located to the presidential limousine's left, she runs southwestward and parallel with the limousine, which she faces for a short time when the limousine is to her direct right.\nPage: Dealey Plaza. Sentence: Dealey Plaza , in the historic West End district of downtown Dallas, Texas (U.S.), is the location of the assassination of John F. Kennedy on November 22, 1963.",
